<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;CHARLES WILLIAM TAYLOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Charles William Taylor is a British watercolorist and illustrator born in 1878, known for his work in the UK and Tunisia, and his deep connection to both places."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNITED KINGDOM OF GREAT BRITAIN AND IRELAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland is the sovereign state that nurtured Taylor's talent and provided the backdrop for his early life and artistic journey."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROYAL COLLEGE OF ART&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Royal College of Art, founded in 1837, is a prestigious institution where Taylor honed his artistic skills and is a testament to his connection to the UK's thriving art scene."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE ILLUSTRATED LONDON NEWS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Illustrated London News is a prominent publication where Taylor's work appeared, further solidifying his status as a British artist."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE TATLER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Tatler is another prominent publication where Taylor's work appeared, contributing to his recognition as a British artist."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE THAMES AT WINDSOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Thames at Windsor is one of Taylor's notable works, showcasing his mastery of watercolor and his deep affection for the British landscape."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROYAL INSTITUTE OF PAINTERS IN WATER COLOURS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Royal Institute of Painters in Water Colours is a prestigious organization that promoted the art form and provided a platform for British artists, of which Taylor was an active member."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUNIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tunis is the bustling city where Taylor lived for nearly a decade, inspired by its rich cultural heritage and warm people, and where he found a new home and family."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUNISIAN SOUKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Tunisian Souks are the vibrant markets where Taylor sat and drew, capturing the essence of North African culture in his art."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FATIMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fatima is the proprietor of a small café in Tunis where Taylor set up his easel, and she and her family took him under their wing, becoming a part of his new home."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CUMIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cumin is a spice that Taylor encountered in Tunis, adding to the sensory experience of his time there."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORIANDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coriander is a spice that Taylor encountered in Tunis, adding to the sensory experience of his time there."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHIRLING DERVISHES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Whirling dervishes are a cultural symbol in Tunisia that inspired Taylor's art, reflecting the spiritual and cultural richness of the region."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREY SKIES OF LONDON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The grey skies of London represent the environment Taylor left behind, contrasting with the golden light of North Africa."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GOLDEN LIGHT OF NORTH AFRICA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The golden light of North Africa represents the new environment Taylor embraced, inspiring his art and personal growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WARM PEOPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Warm people represent the welcoming and supportive community Taylor found in Tunis, contributing to his sense of belonging."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEW FAMILY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"New family represents the close-knit community Taylor formed in Tunis, providing emotional support and inspiration."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WINDING STREETS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Winding streets represent the urban landscape of Tunis, influencing Taylor's artistic compositions and daily life."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MINT TEA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mint tea is a traditional beverage that Taylor enjoyed in Tunis, symbolizing the hospitality and cultural exchange."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMALL CAFÉ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A small café in Tunis is where Taylor set up his easel and met Fatima, serving as a hub for his artistic and social activities."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BUSTLING SOUKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bustling souks are the vibrant markets where Taylor drew, capturing the essence of Tunisian culture and daily life."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPICE MARKET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spice market is a specific area within the souks where Taylor drew, representing the sensory and cultural richness of Tunis."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0410</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;CHARLES WILLIAM TAYLOR&quot;" target="&quot;UNITED KINGDOM OF GREAT BRITAIN AND IRELAND&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Taylor's life and artistic journey were deeply connected to the United Kingdom, which nurtured his talent and provided the backdrop for his work."</data>
      <data key="d5">"nurturing, inspiration"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0410</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CHARLES WILLIAM TAYLOR&quot;" target="&quot;ROYAL COLLEGE OF ART&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Taylor enrolled at the prestigious Royal College of Art, a hub for artistic excellence, highlighting his connection to the UK's thriving art scene."</data>
      <data key="d5">"education, artistic excellence"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0410</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CHARLES WILLIAM TAYLOR&quot;" target="&quot;THE ILLUSTRATED LONDON NEWS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Taylor's work appeared in The Illustrated London News, contributing to his recognition as a British artist."</data>
      <data key="d5">"publication, recognition"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0410</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CHARLES WILLIAM TAYLOR&quot;" target="&quot;THE THAMES AT WINDSOR&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The Thames at Windsor is one of Taylor's notable works, showcasing his mastery of watercolor and his deep affection for the British landscape."</data>
      <data key="d5">"masterpiece, landscape affection"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0410</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CHARLES WILLIAM TAYLOR&quot;" target="&quot;ROYAL INSTITUTE OF PAINTERS IN WATER COLOURS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Taylor was an active member of the Royal Institute of Painters in Water Colours, a prestigious organization that promoted the art form and provided a platform for British artists."</data>
      <data key="d5">"membership, promotion"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0410</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CHARLES WILLIAM TAYLOR&quot;" target="&quot;TUNIS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Taylor lived in Tunis for nearly a decade, finding inspiration and a new home in the rich cultural heritage and warm people of North Africa."</data>
      <data key="d5">"inspiration, new home"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0410</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CHARLES WILLIAM TAYLOR&quot;" target="&quot;TUNISIAN SOUKS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Taylor sat and drew in the Tunisian Souks, capturing the essence of North African culture in his art."</data>
      <data key="d5">"inspiration, cultural reflection"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0410</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CHARLES WILLIAM TAYLOR&quot;" target="&quot;FATIMA&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Fatima and her family took Taylor under their wing in Tunis, becoming a part of his new home and family."</data>
      <data key="d5">"family, support"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0410</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
</graphml>
